[milestone 49] Implementer summary: All changes are left uncommitted in the working tree as instructed. Milestone 49 is complete and genuinely verified. Summary: Added a new syscall 16 (`process::exec_elf()` in `kernel/src/process.rs`, dispatched from `kernel/src/usertest.rs`) that replaces a live process's entire address space — new PML4, new code/stack/heap frames from a freshly-parsed on-disk ELF, real (possibly non-default) entry point — while preserving its pid, open fds, and pgid, reusing the existing `elf.rs` parser and `create_process_from_elf()`'s PML4-rebuild primitive (the same one `fork()` already uses) with zero new unsafe page-table code. The old flat-binary exec (syscall 9) is untouched. I added a boot-time self-test (`self_test_exec_elf` in `process.rs`, wired into `main.rs`) that checks the process's `entry`/`code_frame`/`pml4_frame` fields directly before/after — real proof of a rebuilt address space, not just log-watching — and it passes in a real QEMU boot (`milestones/m49_boot_after_fix.log`). Along the way I found and fixed two real pre-existing bugs left over from Milestone 44: `kernel/assets/testelf_altentry.elf` was a 16-byte placeholder instead of a real ELF, and its source (`tools/testelf_altentry_src/testelf_altentry.rs`) had an off-by-one array-size compile error that's almost certainly why. Full writeup with logs and root-cause evidence is in `milestones/m49_implement.md`.

